                    {
                        "form_id": "3255da91-0b4a-456b-8f4e-94bcd2532859",
                        "entry_id": "9d188720-b6fa-3f74-b9d7-ff079582ceef",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "чужезе́мцах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e67c0fc1-4fc4-3c42-92b3-0a2f20edf44d",
                        "entry_id": "9d188720-b6fa-3f74-b9d7-ff079582ceef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что иностранец; человек из чужой земли, страны"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2b14f0c-55bc-4201-a727-62436413a540",
                                "sense_id": "e67c0fc1-4fc4-3c42-92b3-0a2f20edf44d",
                                "text": "Один из ораторов отметил также, что, чужеземец по рождению, Абулфазл Фазал был подлинным патриотом России и всегда настаивал на особом пути, которым должна идти к счастью его вторая родина."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3969a249-4519-4ead-bd36-0c375ae1c1e5",
                                "sense_id": "e67c0fc1-4fc4-3c42-92b3-0a2f20edf44d",
                                "text": "При этом гость, т. е. человек из иного города или чужеземец, имел первенство перед другими заимодавцами, а за ним князь, потом уже прочие заимодавцы получали остальное."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "72906783-c37b-420c-99f5-6a09055321db",
                        "source_entry_id": "9d188720-b6fa-3f74-b9d7-ff079582ceef",
                        "source_sense_id": "e67c0fc1-4fc4-3c42-92b3-0a2f20edf44d",
                        "target_lang_word": "stranger",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stranger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc69b93b-2e94-37a7-94a7-15b8f2968c54",
                                        "entry_id": "fe106cc3-ed04-3b06-9425-d8cd5857059b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "comparative form of strange: more strange"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "comparative",
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88c7efd4-0b7c-4d94-b799-afb480384d00",
                                                "sense_id": "cc69b93b-2e94-37a7-94a7-15b8f2968c54",
                                                "text": "Truth is stranger than fiction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stranger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71470f70-2877-3d1d-9a99-22c588221bfb",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person whom one does not know; a person who is neither a friend nor an acquaintance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33811bdd-b662-4705-8b22-05aa4ee4d313",
                                                "sense_id": "71470f70-2877-3d1d-9a99-22c588221bfb",
                                                "text": "That gentleman is a stranger to me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd86ff50-5347-44c0-90fe-6bb17ffc1764",
                                                "sense_id": "71470f70-2877-3d1d-9a99-22c588221bfb",
                                                "text": "Children are taught not to talk to strangers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8197f7c5-9dfc-4b4e-ab65-5c63837f9da8",
                                                "sense_id": "71470f70-2877-3d1d-9a99-22c588221bfb",
                                                "text": "In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for its own select circle, a club, or society, of habitués, who met every evening, for a pipe and a cheerful glass.[…]Strangers might enter the room, but they were made to feel that they were there on sufferance: they were received with distance and suspicion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f231d287-2e90-41a8-abc8-b16aee1e168e",
                                                "sense_id": "71470f70-2877-3d1d-9a99-22c588221bfb",
                                                "text": "Our love (our love, our love) / Our love is in danger (danger) / And if you don't hurry home / I might give it to a stranger"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d8cdd05-8c7c-303d-9ae5-42aace57c8bc",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outsider or foreigner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6885fe6-91dc-452a-9afb-75f794083fd2",
                                                "sense_id": "7d8cdd05-8c7c-303d-9ae5-42aace57c8bc",
                                                "text": "I am a most poor woman and a stranger, / Born out of your dominions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cad67876-4b46-4d62-9009-d73ccf5b5803",
                                                "sense_id": "7d8cdd05-8c7c-303d-9ae5-42aace57c8bc",
                                                "text": "Melons on beds of ice are taught to bear, / And strangers to the sun yet ripen here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a87f97c-6288-4723-a36e-6f3e5442e0a5",
                                                "sense_id": "7d8cdd05-8c7c-303d-9ae5-42aace57c8bc",
                                                "text": "I like to be a stranger myself—it was my destiny; but I wish to be the only stranger."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc8fdbd5-3856-30e7-9ef7-773231a76ecd",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One not admitted to communion or fellowship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4229b64b-15c3-3362-abf7-9c9e26777de3",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A newcomer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccc41f6d-57fd-441e-95c5-0d41a5697edb",
                                                "sense_id": "4229b64b-15c3-3362-abf7-9c9e26777de3",
                                                "text": "[…] St. Bede's at this period of its history was perhaps the poorest and most miserable parish in the East End of London. Close-packed, crushed by the buttressed height of the railway viaduct, rendered airless by huge walls of factories, it at once banished lively interest from a stranger's mind and left only a dull oppression of the spirit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fdfac33-000d-44ec-88ce-85ad9b5cb0c6",
                                                "sense_id": "4229b64b-15c3-3362-abf7-9c9e26777de3",
                                                "text": "The first thing that strikes the stranger is the sharpness of the curves on the metre gauge; it is not unusual for a long train to be travelling in three directions at once, and the engine is frequently in full view of the windows of the ninth or tenth carriage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1cf2126-5192-4c5d-893f-81dfd58fd51b",
                                                "sense_id": "4229b64b-15c3-3362-abf7-9c9e26777de3",
                                                "text": "Wearing number 66 for his club side, Alexander-Arnold is no stranger to an unusual shirt number. Regardless, the sight of the right-back wearing 10 in central midfield for England was guaranteed to catch the eye."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a46ac7f-577b-3209-a3b0-7447ac2d1f4b",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used ironically to refer to a person who the speaker knows."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7df739d-e207-4508-b4ef-236e70448756",
                                                "sense_id": "4a46ac7f-577b-3209-a3b0-7447ac2d1f4b",
                                                "text": "Hello, stranger!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fa02eb9-fd67-37de-9e60-430b9feaf11e",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One not belonging to the family or household; a guest; a visitor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "507e0232-add7-4304-825f-5e255e82366f",
                                                "sense_id": "3fa02eb9-fd67-37de-9e60-430b9feaf11e",
                                                "text": "To honour and receive / Our heavenly stranger."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd731a08-2cd4-3ad9-8f93-019204238a76",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One not privy or party to an act, contract, or title; a mere intruder or intermeddler; one who interferes without right."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc29fb18-98ba-4f43-bc00-228d9454bf77",
                                                "sense_id": "cd731a08-2cd4-3ad9-8f93-019204238a76",
                                                "text": "Actual possession of land gives a good title against a stranger having no title."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69243a48-575e-40ec-9e17-a31f95015610",
                                                "sense_id": "cd731a08-2cd4-3ad9-8f93-019204238a76",
                                                "text": "[Judge Beverly] Davis then granted the adoption to the new wife of the boy's father; this action designated the boy's natural mother a \"legal stranger,\" terminating all rights the mother had to visit her child."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c17e6ae-019d-361f-994e-9248e52b7510",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39e65-b19c-3eca-9f15-dff541d5780b",
                                        "glosses": [
